00:01:55.210 --> 00:01:56.640
washing people's cars,

00:01:56.640 --> 00:01:59.870
selling juice and lemonade and candy.

00:01:59.870 --> 00:02:02.183
It was always to do a hustle.

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:07.610
Somewhere along that time in New Jersey,

00:02:07.610 --> 00:02:11.130
sports cards became a
very big thing in America,

00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:13.840
baseball cards, American football cards,

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:15.800
and I started collecting them

00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:18.560
and by the time I was 1314 years old,

00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:23.560
I was making one to $3,000 a
weekend as a 13 year old child,

00:02:23.690 --> 00:02:24.860
which you can imagine,

00:02:24.860 --> 00:02:27.300
feels like you're a millionaire.

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:30.050
Eventually my dad worked very hard

00:02:30.050 --> 00:02:31.220
and saved all his money

00:02:31.220 --> 00:02:34.250
and he bought a small
liquor store in New Jersey.

00:02:34.250 --> 00:02:37.510
I was forced to work in that store.

00:02:37.510 --> 00:02:41.380
And that is really where
I started my real career.

00:02:41.380 --> 00:02:45.480
I fell in love with the idea of knowing

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:49.370
